{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads","id":655833,"title":"Questions About Glitches And Demonic Powers I Haven't Seen In Other Threads","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-07T19:26:41-07:00","id":655833,"title":"Questions About Glitches And Demonic Powers I Haven't Seen In Other Threads","content":"Do Embeds, Exploits and Gadgets stack with Merits and other mundane sources of dice bonuses?<br /> <br /> Does a Demon need to know an Embed or Exploit before Installing it into a Gadget? You probably do need the original power if you are building a Demonic Form Gadget, and you can uninstall Gadgets to learn the Embeds, Exploits and Demonic Forms inside them. But I am not sure if you could make a laser cannon without knowing the Hellfire Exploit first, or an Angel detecting radar without knowing the Voice Of The Machine Embed.<br /> <br /> Can you combine Demonic Forms, Embeds and Exploits? For example, a Destroyer is ambushed, and Down &amp; Dirty Combat is not an option. Could he combine his Rivet Arm Modification with the Merciless Gunman Embed and Hellfire Exploit? That would let him shoot the enemies with +3A and 8 Again (Rote Quality if the activation of Merciless Gunman gets an Exceptional Success)?<br /> <br /> Can Spoofing, Going Native, Deep Cover and similar powers temporarily hide Glitches? Brands and Emanations might be hidden with these powers, but Tells might just require a Subterfuge or Persuasion roll to explain away as mundane habits. If it is possible, I'm guessing that it must be very exhausting, thus requiring additional Aether, 1 willpower point, dice penalties or any combination thereof.<br /> <br /> Can restoration facilities cure the permanent Glitches caused by increasing Primum and suffering a Dramatic Failure on a Compromise roll? From what I've gathered, yes. So, can a Demon with Primum 9 and who fails Compromise rolls often enter a restoration facility and come out with no Glitches at all? I do know that restoration facilities are very well guarded, I just want to be sure if I'm reading the rules correctly.<br /> <br /> Is there an upper limit for how many Glitches a Demon can have? If so, what happens if he exceeds that limit? I think it could be interesting if too many Glitches caused Aggravated damage that can only be healed with mundane Medicine rolls or waiting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-07-2015, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:39:46-07:00","id":655939,"title":"","content":"The following is all just my interpretation, so I won't be providing sources or page numbers.<br /> <br /> Does a Demon need to know an Embed or Exploit before Installing it into a Gadget? Yes. It doesn't really make any sense otherwise, how can you make an object that utilizes a backdoor pathway in the rules of reality if you don't <i>know</i> those backdoors?<br /> <br /> Can you combine Demonic Forms, Embeds and Exploits? Of course. There's no reason you shouldn't be able to.<br /> <br /> Can Spoofing, Going Native, Deep Cover and similar powers temporarily hide Glitches? No. The whole point of glitches is that they stick with you, and none of those abilities explicitly say they bypass that general rule.<br /> <br /> Can restoration facilities cure the permanent Glitches caused by increasing Primum and suffering a Dramatic Failure on a Compromise roll? I believe so. They cure glitches, and it doesn't state anywhere that there's a limitation for 'Permanent' Glitches. It makes restoration facilities a high value target for powerful demons with lots of glitches, which has a lot of story potential in my mind. If you're stuck with a temporary glitch, why would you hunt down Infrastructure to remove it when you could just hunker down in your safehouse for a day or two? I'd say Permanent glitches are probably the main meta-reason that those facilities are a thing.<br /> <br /> Is there an upper limit for how many Glitches a Demon can have? No, I don't think so. It's never mentioned anywhere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T01:05:13-07:00","id":656201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads#post655833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Embeds, Exploits and Gadgets stack with Merits and other mundane sources of dice bonuses?</div> </div> </div> </div> It depends on the power in question. Sometimes, they stack, sometimes not. I usually err on the side of what's fun, and then what's internally consistant. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does a Demon need to know an Embed or Exploit before Installing it into a Gadget? </div> </div> </div> Absolutely<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you combine Demonic Forms, Embeds and Exploits? For example, a Destroyer is ambushed, and Down &amp; Dirty Combat is not an option. Could he combine his Rivet Arm Modification with the Merciless Gunman Embed and Hellfire Exploit? That would let him shoot the enemies with +3A and 8 Again (Rote Quality if the activation of Merciless Gunman gets an Exceptional Success)? </div> </div> </div> Sure. There are some people who claim that the Rivert Arm isn't a gun, so isn't viable, but there are other examples of combining embed/exploits with demon form abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Spoofing, Going Native, Deep Cover and similar powers temporarily hide Glitches? Brands and Emanations might be hidden with these powers, but Tells might just require a Subterfuge or Persuasion roll to explain away as mundane habits. If it is possible, I'm guessing that it must be very exhausting, thus requiring additional Aether, 1 willpower point, dice penalties or any combination thereof. </div> </div> </div> I generally say no to all of them. Its a flaw in the Cover's appearance, and no amount of demon magic can cover it. You CAN use mundane methods to hide it (and the one Embed for changing clothes, since that's indirect), but its unthematic for something like this to be handwaved away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can restoration facilities cure the permanent Glitches caused by increasing Primum and suffering a Dramatic Failure on a Compromise roll? From what I've gathered, yes. So, can a Demon with Primum 9 and who fails Compromise rolls often enter a restoration facility and come out with no Glitches at all? I do know that restoration facilities are very well guarded, I just want to be sure if I'm reading the rules correctly. </div> </div> </div> Restoration facilities can fix them, but the high Primum would just naturally create the glitches again - the Covers just aren't powerful enough to hide the demon's true nature anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there an upper limit for how many Glitches a Demon can have? If so, what happens if he exceeds that limit? I think it could be interesting if too many Glitches caused Aggravated damage that can only be healed with mundane Medicine rolls or waiting. </div> </div> </div> In theory, no. Realistically, he would attract angelic attention since a casual observer would notice that the character isn't human, and thus quickly suffer compromise checks (via &quot;revealing true nature&quot; compromises) that flag you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:39:30-07:00","id":658516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=656201#post656201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Restoration facilities can fix them, but the high Primum would just naturally create the glitches again - the Covers just aren't powerful enough to hide the demon's true nature anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still gotta disagree here. After rereading Demon today, it explicitly says that permanent glitches can be fixed by Restoration facilities, and it makes no mention of the glitches coming back. If it <i>didn't </i>permanently fix them:<br /> <br /> 1) There's no need for it be able to fix them at all, much less call that out explicitly as a solution, because they'll just come back.<br /> 2) There's no need for restoration facilities to exist. Infiltrating one is explicitly a dangerous affair, and transient glitches all fade within a day or two if your Primum is 5 or less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:55:49-07:00","id":658566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads#post655833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Spoofing, Going Native, Deep Cover and similar powers temporarily hide Glitches? Brands and Emanations might be hidden with these powers, but Tells might just require a Subterfuge or Persuasion roll to explain away as mundane habits. If it is possible, I'm guessing that it must be very exhausting, thus requiring additional Aether, 1 willpower point, dice penalties or any combination thereof.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Spoofing:</b> No, not any more than you could partially manifest a rivet gun and then spoof to make people not notice it. Spoofing just deflects the use of supernatural abilities to detect the Unchained as supernatural beings. A glitch is not somebody else using a sensory power, it's an overflow problem you need to deal with personally, either by hiding it normally and waiting it out or by repairing it. Deep Cover just expands the versatility of spoofing, and so is also of no use here.<br /> <br /> <b>Going Native:</b> Yes, I would allow Going Native to suppress glitches. They will come back when the power expires, and I'd freeze the timer on temporary glitches for the duration so you'd still have to wait those out as a demon, but Going Native genuinely makes you a mortal human for its duration. Mortal humans do not normally suffer glitches, and Going Native has enough drawbacks and dangers to its use that it generally ought to be very effective at the one thing it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads#post655833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can restoration facilities cure the permanent Glitches caused by increasing Primum and suffering a Dramatic Failure on a Compromise roll? From what I've gathered, yes. So, can a Demon with Primum 9 and who fails Compromise rolls often enter a restoration facility and come out with no Glitches at all? I do know that restoration facilities are very well guarded, I just want to be sure if I'm reading the rules correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Permanent glitches incurred by compromise: absolutely yes. Most temporary glitches are short-lived enough that it's simply not worth finding a facility. Infiltrating a facility is enough of a big deal that, yes, it ought to be able to patch you up from ongoing glitches from compromise.<br /> <br /> Permanent glitches acquired by high Primum: I would say no. Compromise glitches result from a short-circuit of your Cover: they can be traced to a cause and corrected. Primum glitches result from having such strong Primum that it overflows past the human seeming of Cover. It's a narrative drawback attached to surpassing power, similarly to vampires' need for increasingly potent vitae and werewolves' growing need to hunt and consume. It's coming from inside the house.<br /> <br /> There is a way to get rid of Primum glitches: reduce your Primum below the glitch threshold (which ought to be something that can be done by hijacking facilities in a similar manner). If you try to strip the glitch without reducing your Primum, your overflowing Primum is going to need another release vent. If it's not a new glitch to replace the old one, it's probably even worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T05:10:02-07:00","id":660601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=658516#post658516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still gotta disagree here. After rereading Demon today, it explicitly says that permanent glitches can be fixed by Restoration facilities, and it makes no mention of the glitches coming back. If it <i>didn't </i>permanently fix them:</div> </div> </div> </div> From the core book:<br /> <br /> &quot;A high Primum isn\u2019t the only way for demons to acquire glitches; among other things, failing a compromise roll (see p. 115) or the use of certain supernatural powers may earn a demon a glitch. The key difference is that those glitches can usually be repaired. Glitches acquired by raising Primum are permanent parts of the demon unless some effect drops their Primum rating.&quot; DtD p155.<br /> <br /> There are multiple ways of gaining a permanent glitch, not just high Primum. Restoration fascilities can fix the non-Primum based ones, and fascilities are known for their ability to degrade Primum, so technically, the restoration fascilities can fix the high Primum problems, but at a cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T11:11:43-07:00","id":663291,"title":"","content":"As for the high primum I think we got in lengthy discussion about glitches and came to the idea that restoration facilities can't repair high primum glitches. Though it be a fun story to find the esoteric means of doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T15:00:27-07:00","id":675730,"title":"","content":"I have some more questions.<br /> <br /> Can you spend willpower on rolls for Compromise, Legend and Spoofing? If yes, does it grant +2 or +3? None of these rolls involve Resistance Attributes, so I'd say +3.<br /> <br /> What might be the results of a Dramatic Failure or an Exceptional Success on the roll to generate a Legend?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T18:51:01-07:00","id":675898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=675730#post675730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some more questions.<br /> <br /> Can you spend willpower on rolls for Compromise, Legend and Spoofing? If yes, does it grant +2 or +3? None of these rolls involve Resistance Attributes, so I'd say +3.<br /> <br /> What might be the results of a Dramatic Failure or an Exceptional Success on the roll to generate a Legend?</div> </div> </div> </div> Generally, you can't spend willpower on Integrity equivalent degeneration, but I don't see anything that says no in this case, so it might be an exception (akin to spending wp to make an Exploit not cause Compromise). Personally, I wouldn't allow it because spending willpower represents putting extra effort into an action. How are you putting extra effort into the God-Machine's notice? It doesn't make sense in this context to me. <br /> <br /> Yes, you can spend it on Legend and Spoofing. At least, I have always allowed it and never seen anything to the contrary.<br /> <br /> Its always +3. The only time you ever get +2 is if you're temporarily boosting your score by 2 when its being subtracted. Never when its a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-23-2015, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T22:31:16-07:00","id":677331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=675898#post675898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Generally, you can't spend willpower on Integrity equivalent degeneration, but I don't see anything that says no in this case, so it might be an exception (akin to spending wp to make an Exploit not cause Compromise). Personally, I wouldn't allow it because spending willpower represents putting extra effort into an action. How are you putting extra effort into the God-Machine's notice? It doesn't make sense in this context to me.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can spend it on Legend and Spoofing. At least, I have always allowed it and never seen anything to the contrary.<br /> <br /> Its always +3. The only time you ever get +2 is if you're temporarily boosting your score by 2 when its being subtracted. Never when its a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, rolling for the degeneration of Humanity/Harmony/Wisdom requires you to roll a specific number of dice associated with the &quot;sin&quot; in question. However, rolls for Compromise don't follow a hierarchy of &quot;sins&quot;. I do think that allowing willpower expenditure might make Compromise rolls rather easy to succeed. Despite that, I'd allow a willpower point to be spent to negate the -3 penalty to Compromise for assuming full Demonic Form. You can keep spending willpower each scene, but since each scene imposes an additional -1 penalty for Compromise, you will still suffer penalties.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T23:12:47-07:00","id":677336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=677331#post677331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, rolling for the degeneration of Humanity/Harmony/Wisdom requires you to roll a specific number of dice associated with the &quot;sin&quot; in question. However, rolls for Compromise don't follow a hierarchy of &quot;sins&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's mostly first edition design, I'd say. Vampire still holds to it, but 2e Harmony rolls a normal dice pool (with the specification that you can't add dice with Willpower), and 2e Integrity functions very similarly to Cover, both using a dice pool and lacking a specific list of breaking points.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's a big deal which call you make on this one, whether you allow spending Willpower on compromise risks or not. I'd probably lean towards no, but I don't think the game breaks if you allow it. Same with Spoofing.<br /> <br /> I'd probably specifically allow it on rolls to create a Legend, though I'm generally not a fan of the Legend rules. They're sufficiently strict that they don't really feel like a viable option in the first place. I'd love to hear if anybody's had play experience to the contrary, though. Maybe they're more useful for demons who find themselves maintaining several Covers and hotswapping between them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T04:35:16-07:00","id":677486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=677336#post677336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably specifically allow it on rolls to create a Legend, though I'm generally not a fan of the Legend rules. They're sufficiently strict that they don't really feel like a viable option in the first place. I'd love to hear if anybody's had play experience to the contrary, though. Maybe they're more useful for demons who find themselves maintaining several Covers and hotswapping between them?</div> </div> </div> </div> I used the Legend rules all the time. Spend 1 aether for free skill dots or merits? Sounds great. There's even an Embed to make it last longer.<br /> <br /> The only part that's strict about Legend is the Imposter Condition, which basically states that you &quot;feel hollow&quot; and give a cumulative -1 penalty to further rolls. If you spend time tapping into your Cover's medical training all the time, you'll eventually start learning medicine. Its just a way to encourage eventually &quot;becoming the mask.&quot; Spend too much time in Cover, and you eventually become the Cover in personality and outlook. Its how many angels Fell in the first place.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T05:34:34-07:00","id":677526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=677336#post677336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's mostly first edition design, I'd say. Vampire still holds to it, but 2e Harmony rolls a normal dice pool (with the specification that you can't add dice with Willpower), and 2e Integrity functions very similarly to Cover, both using a dice pool and lacking a specific list of breaking points.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's a big deal which call you make on this one, whether you allow spending Willpower on compromise risks or not. I'd probably lean towards no, but I don't think the game breaks if you allow it. Same with Spoofing.<br /> <br /> I'd probably specifically allow it on rolls to create a Legend, though I'm generally not a fan of the Legend rules. They're sufficiently strict that they don't really feel like a viable option in the first place. I'd love to hear if anybody's had play experience to the contrary, though. Maybe they're more useful for demons who find themselves maintaining several Covers and hotswapping between them?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't find the rules for Legend all that harsh. And if you consider the Persistent Legend Embed, it becomes more viable as a way to quickly get Merits and Skills. <br /> <br /> If you want the rules to be less strict, I'd say if you get a Dramatic Failure on the roll to generate the Legend, the cumulative penalty caused by the Impostor Condition is reset. Getting an Exceptional Success on the Legend roll also resets that penalty, but you don't gain the Cover Beat that you'd have received if you purchased the real Skill or Merit. However, choosing to make the Legend roll a Dramatic Failure calls for a Compromise roll. Additionally, you could rule that another way to Resolve the Impostor Condition is to circumvent your problems without using Legends for one chapter. That makes the Demon feel more resourceful and smart, which helps to fight the feelings of hollowness.<br /> <br /> Also, I have another question. Characters inside the Astral Realms look like how they imagine themselves to look. If a Demon used Rip The Gates to enter the Astral, does he end up looking like his Demonic Form, or does the Cover stay strong? I'd say that Demons with a Cover of 6+ don't suffer any inconvenience in that regard, but if their Cover is 5 or lower, they become easier to track through the Astral, as they leave behind trails that clever Astral travelers can identify. This is not a problem with the Demon's emotional self-control, but a problem with his Cover. Also, when they enter the portal to the Astral, where exactly do they emerge? Their Oneiros? Somewhere on the Temenos or Anima Mundi similar to the place they just left? Can they choose between these three destinations? As for what they can do in the Astral, I'd say they follow the same rules Mages do. In other words, they don't gain the ability to transform their surroundings with their thoughts. They will have to use Embeds, Exploits and so on, like Mages have to use their spells. Unlike Mages, who don't suffer Paradox inside the Astral, Demons still suffer Compromises.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T08:15:53-07:00","id":677637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=677526#post677526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I have another question. Characters inside the Astral Realms look like how they imagine themselves to look. If a Demon used Rip The Gates to enter the Astral, does he end up looking like his Demonic Form, or does the Cover stay strong?</div> </div> </div> </div> The point of a Cover is to appear as a normal human. Appearing as anything but a normal human would be counter productive for a demon. I see no reason to make things difficult or troublesome in that way - you're just mechanically discouraging visiting the Astral at that point. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd say that Demons with a Cover of 6+ don't suffer any inconvenience in that regard, but if their Cover is 5 or lower, they become easier to track through the Astral, as they leave behind trails that clever Astral travelers can identify. </div> </div> </div> What does being easier to track have to do with accumulation of reality glitches? Especially for someone unfamiliar with demons and angels? Why should an Unchained in Demon Form (effectively no Cover) be really easy to track? Its not like actors in the Astral remember things like that, they just play parts. And the demon isn't exactly leaking breadcrumbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T09:01:49-07:00","id":677668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=677637#post677637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The point of a Cover is to appear as a normal human. Appearing as anything but a normal human would be counter productive for a demon. I see no reason to make things difficult or troublesome in that way - you're just mechanically discouraging visiting the Astral at that point.<br /> <br /> What does being easier to track have to do with accumulation of reality glitches? Especially for someone unfamiliar with demons and angels? Why should an Unchained in Demon Form (effectively no Cover) be really easy to track? Its not like actors in the Astral remember things like that, they just play parts. And the demon isn't exactly leaking breadcrumbs.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair points. It seems I often misinterpret or incorrectly remember the nature of Covers. Thanks for clearing that up again.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T16:49:41-07:00","id":678288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=677526#post677526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Characters inside the Astral Realms look like how they imagine themselves to look. If a Demon used Rip The Gates to enter the Astral, does he end up looking like his Demonic Form, or does the Cover stay strong?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that's a manifestation of the dream form most characters assume when they enter the Astral Realms. It's fluid in appearance because it's not their physical body, but a psychic projection of their identity. If a demon were to enter the Astral Realms in dream form, such as with the assistance of a mage, I'd say his Cover would remain intact, but fluid appearance would take off from there \u2013 so a demon with Cover as a mercenary would appear in the Astral the same way the mercenary would if he weren't a demon. Rip the Gates simplifies this further: it opens a physical gate into the Astral Realms. You're just walking in with your normal body, so you look the same you would anywhere else, complete with ability to switch Covers on the fly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=677526#post677526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what they can do in the Astral, I'd say they follow the same rules Mages do. In other words, they don't gain the ability to transform their surroundings with their thoughts. They will have to use Embeds, Exploits and so on, like Mages have to use their spells. Unlike Mages, who don't suffer Paradox inside the Astral, Demons still suffer Compromises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, sounds about right to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T10:10:34-07:00","id":703639,"title":"","content":"New question. Would there be anything problematic about letting the Hellfire Exploit apply to melee weapons as well as firearms (and use melee weapons as hardware for a Hellfire Gadget)? I always did want to use it conjunction with the Blade Hand Modification. However, a Demon combining the two would have have to spend 1 willpower point on each attack to avoid compromise from the use of an Exploit, in addition to the point of Aether. Not to mention that there is already Cavernous Maw, which deals +2A by default and doesn't cause compromise if used in a partial transformation. A Demon could just have a Blade Hand and use Hellfire with it to deal +4A, and probably not take Cavernous Maw as a Process (biting chunks of flesh off might not be his style, either). What if Cavernous Maw also had Armor Piercing [Primum/2 round up]? Besides not requiring willpower to cancel a compromise roll, that alteration might make it more appealing as an option for melee combat.<br /> <br /> Another Process I'd like to change would be Body Modification. Instead of swapping dots between Physical Attributes with the Powerstat cap still present, the Demon would have a pool of dots equal to Primum to reflexively distribute among them and his attribute maximum would be one dot higher than the one normally allowed by Primum. However, each Physical Attribute cannot have more than +5 with this new version. A Demon with this Process who Goes Loud would be a combat powerhouse. Maybe require Aether expenditure for this version, to keep things balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-16-2015, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T12:10:31-07:00","id":703689,"title":"","content":"I'd say no to Hellfire, RAW, but yes to making a Near Field Gadget using Hellfire (that's what Near Field is for, after all). Such a usable power might easily be an Interlock, though.<br /> <br /> Not sure how well the free dots would be quasi-balance-wise. It <i>is</i> a Process, though, so should be competitive vs the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T05:52:56-07:00","id":706684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=703639#post703639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question. Would there be anything problematic about letting the Hellfire Exploit apply to melee weapons as well as firearms (and use melee weapons as hardware for a Hellfire Gadget)?</div> </div> </div> </div> The exploit explicitly only applies to firearms, but I think it'd be fine to make a Hellfire Sword gadget. Actually, I'd make it a second tier lambda sword, using Combustion, Hellfire, and Incindiary.<br /> <br /> The only thing &quot;problematic&quot; with making the Expliot work on a sword is that it feels kind of unthematic for DtD. Swords are basically glorified metal clubs, and demon powers are all into the whole spy-technology thing. A giant flaming sword just isn't assassin-y or sniper-ish, and a sword isn't very advanced technology, being a glorified metal club. Would it be unbalanced from a mechanical perspective or cosmological perspective? Not really. So, if you can get your ST to approve using the Exploit on your Blade Hand (some don't want Hellfire to apply even to the bolter gun thing), shouldn't be too much of an issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if Cavernous Maw also had Armor Piercing [Primum/2 round up]? Besides not requiring willpower to cancel a compromise roll, that alteration might make it more appealing as an option for melee combat. </div> </div> </div> Against what, excactly? Biting is a grapple style move, and generally speaking, armor doesn't matter when you're biting an unprotected throat. Angels are the big combat threat in DtD, and, generally speaking, they don't have or need armor. Against another combat-demon, they likely use Just Bruised as well, so the Armor Piercing isn't really necessary either. In all honesty, if you want a Grapple-Demon (which is pretty unreliable as a tactic in DtD given certain abilities), there are several Demon Form stuff you'll be taking, including Acidic Spit, which stacks on more damage, which just gets insane. Claws can be used as part of the grapple to add weapon bonus, Extra Limbs and Strength for leverage, and so on. After a point, that Armor Piercing ends up becoming nothing more than +2 auto-damage against armored opponents, which will be either 1) redundant against non-combatant characters, or 2) a bit excessive as a combat thing against combat characters.<br /> <br /> And the main use of Cavernous Maw isn't combat, its being able to eat and destroy anything you want. You can eat evidence of a crime, chew through buildings, you name it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another Process I'd like to change would be Body Modification. Instead of swapping dots between Physical Attributes with the Powerstat cap still present, the Demon would have a pool of dots equal to Primum to reflexively distribute among them and his attribute maximum would be one dot higher than the one normally allowed by Primum. However, each Physical Attribute cannot have more than +5 with this new version. A Demon with this Process who Goes Loud would be a combat powerhouse. Maybe require Aether expenditure for this version, to keep things balanced. </div> </div> </div> Ehhh.... one of the things that prevents Going Loud from being too outragously broken is that it only boosts your Primum as a stat, nothing else. I'm going to have to say that this is nothing more than pushing to make Bigger-Badder-Combat-Monsters. Body Modification lets you swap from being a powerhouse, to a stealthy infiltrator, to someone who can shrug off anything. I see no reason to do this other than give more combat power, and that's not a good reason to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-18-2015, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:56:07-08:00","id":760301,"title":"","content":"New question. The Nanobot Composition Process allows you to create objects and simple machines from his body. You can't change your total Size, but could a Demon transform things other than his hands and other extremities? Could he transform his head, or even his entire torso into a machine? If paired with the Huge Size Modification, could the Demon transform into a small vehicle like a motorcycle? If so, should this require a roll and/other Aether? What exactly would count as simple for a techno-arcane monster? A &quot;mere&quot; Modification or Technology can do impressive things, and the most advanced electronics on Earth are basic compared to a lot of Infrastructure. The limitation that I'm sure of is that Nanobot Composition can only create weapons or potentially harmful objects with a Damage Bonus of +0L. If the player wants an effective weapon for the Demonic Form, he can pick Blade Hand, Rivet Arm, Eliminator Cannon, Cavernous Maw and so on.<br /> <br /> I also think that the ability to ignore <b>all</b> damage with 1 Aether per ignored attack kind of makes other Demonic Form powers meant for protection look less desirable. Sure, Nanobot Composition can't protect you from flamethrowers, explosives or just a big enough club. Since being made of nanobots is like being a swarm, I'd say that spending 1 Aether allows you to treat parts of your body as if they belonged to a Swarm. More specifically, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/599-zombie-creation-system-from-antagonists-updated-to-gmc?p=363044#post363044\"><b>Swarms as house-ruled by Claire Redfield:</b></a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/599-zombie-creation-system-from-antagonists-updated-to-gmc?p=363044#post363044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Fighting The Swarm</b></span><br /> <br /> Swarms are difficult to harm. After rolling attacks against the swarm as normal, factoring in armor and other modifiers, the swarm takes one point of damage of the appropriate type, or two points with an exceptional success. Damage suffered reduces its Health. Fire, explosions, chemical sprays and other area effects cause normal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Therefore, combining Nanobot Composition with Armored Plates, Tough As Stone and Aegis Protocol would be an effective protection all-around, rather than a bit redundant. You'll still burn through Aether quickly if a lot of enemies are attacking you in a single turn, but Demons always roll Primum to generate a few points of Aether when they run out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-07-2015, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T16:19:19-08:00","id":760314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=760301#post760301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question. The Nanobot Composition Process allows you to create objects and simple machines from his body. [\u2026] What exactly would count as simple for a techno-arcane monster? A &quot;mere&quot; Modification or Technology can do impressive things, and the most advanced electronics on Earth are basic compared to a lot of Infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Today I learned that not everybody was taught what a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simple_machine\" target=\"_blank\">simple machine</a> was in elementary school.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'll still burn through Aether quickly if a lot of enemies are attacking you in a single turn, but Demons always roll Primum to generate a few points of Aether when they run out. </div> </div> </div>Aetheric Bleed is not to be ignored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T10:41:38-08:00","id":760749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=760301#post760301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that the ability to ignore <b>all</b> damage with 1 Aether per ignored attack kind of makes other Demonic Form powers meant for protection look less desirable.</div> </div> </div> </div> In general, dealing pure damage in Demon is overrated. I can remove a target from existance with an extended roll, no direct damage, and undo everything he did the last few minutes. I can trap someone outside time. I can kill someone with a look, or turn them into a statue with a single word. <br /> <br /> Demon, more than any other game, doesn't handle white room theory fights well, because the game gives you so many ways around getting involved in it, its not funny. Seriously, The Look Embed can take your biggest, baddest combat character after Going Loud, look into their eyes, and freeze them in place, slowly killing them with no way to resist. And that's an <i>embed</i>, no aether cost or innate compromise check. <br /> <br /> I don't care about Nanobot Composition, because my Messenger just used the Word to freeze you in place, then proceeds to literally talk you to death. My Guardian just Echoing Death'd your swarm out of existance. My Psychopomp just used <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Reality Enforcement on the Nanobots, forcing all magic powers to stop functioning. </span></span>My Destroyer had lots of fire-form abilities, so just gave your swarm a hug, combined with Combustion and Incindiary. <br /> <br /> And that's before we get into the fact that Nanobot Composition doesn't let you form swarms by default. You can reconfigure your body to have useful gear on you all the time, but that's different from turning into a Swarm. If you want a swarm, we have another Demonic Form ability just for that - <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Insect Swarm, DtD 206. If you really want to turn parts of your body into a swarm... well, go ahead. That won't stop a flaming sword Lambda (using Incindiary and Combustion) carving through parts of your body NOT in swarm form. Or any of the above tactics from working.</span></span><br /> <br /> I find it rather notable that you're worried about the power of an ability that requires no less than 2 separate houserules to work this way. Demon comes with its own swarm rules already, after all. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Therefore, combining Nanobot Composition with Armored Plates, Tough As Stone and Aegis Protocol would be an effective protection all-around, rather than a bit redundant. You'll still burn through Aether quickly if a lot of enemies are attacking you in a single turn, but Demons always roll Primum to generate a few points of Aether when they run out. </div> </div> </div> Putting aside that Aether Bleed is a thing, defense twinking has its limits in that you're far less capable in other roles, you're not going to be walking around with that on all the time. If you fall back on to all that at every fight, that's a lot of compromise checks, which summon powerful groups of cultists and angels on your tail. And even all that won't save you from even three angels coordinating Blast Numina; and that's the most basic of tactics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T12:20:09-08:00","id":760838,"title":"","content":"I'd just like to thank everyone who took the time to reply to this thread so far. I'm starting to feel a little ashamed of my obsession with game balance and white room scenarios. I should focus more on stuff that might cause too much thematic overlap between the narrative niches of the splats. For example, a vampire Discipline that controls fire? Even I know that's not a good idea. A Discipline that controls ice is more thematic, and there's a fan-made one called <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OPkyZ5qBbzhMR11yJzkBCTpGB7Usv5-_UUzKahVwMuE/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Frigus.</b></a><br /> <br /> Come to think of it...I might start a thread for fights that are NOT white rooms. I could come up with different arenas and advantages for either side to keep things interesting, and roll my dice to see where it goes. I could pass it off as some kind of in-universe TV show (animated, probably) complete with narrators, like that homebrewed changeling sport of <a href=\"http://mrparaduo.deviantart.com/art/CtL-Goblin-Ball-451115528\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Goblin Ball.</b></a> Heck, some fights might have unexpected endings.<br /> <br /> Would anyone be interested in such a thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T19:11:59-08:00","id":762756,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this question is stupid, so please bear with me.<br /> <br /> Can a Demon keep his clothes on after assuming full Demonic Form? Many Demonic Forms have spikes, extra arms and other features that would not fit inside, or even destroy normal clothing. I feel like house-ruling that they can do it simply by willing it, and that the clothes adapt automatically. Entering full Demonic Form already generates Aether and heals both bashing and lethal damage. Extending a minor, transforming force field or something similar to the clothes doesn't sound like a stretch.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T20:48:12-08:00","id":762806,"title":"","content":"The demon does keep clothing as the transformation is not physical shapeshifting they cease to be the cover and the demonic form takes its' place. A demon exists as all covers and forms and wears one at a time, simply switching without transformation or fanfare","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3839-crytofloragardener","name":"CrytofloraGardener","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T13:34:26-08:00","id":770922,"title":"","content":"Since Demons don't have any involuntary reactions, are they affected by drunkenness like mortals (i.e. penalty to Mental and Physical, but bonus to Social)? They might get a bonus to fool a drunk person with Subterfuge, I believe. Since they are biologically human when in Cover, I imagine that they can still suffer alcohol poisoning and the like.<br /> <br /> Related to the above: do Demons purify themselves of poisons and diseases when they enter Demonic Form? Do mental illnesses, psychological traumas, addictions and such transfer from Cover to Cover? I imagine Guilty, Spooked, Frightened and the like would, but what about Addiction? Isn't the brain of each body belonging to a Cover separate from the rest, or is the mind of the Demon somehow stuck with certain Conditions and Tilts?<br /> <br /> Can a Demon's Total Control and Liar's Tongue be short-circuited by the mind control powers of other splats, like Auspex and the Mind Arcanum?<br /> <br /> Also, I'd like some second opinions on my question about clothes and Demonic Form above. In any case, Demons could make clothes that adapt to their Demonic Forms as minor Gadgets, like the outfits of the Fantastic Four.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T18:37:18-08:00","id":771119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=770922#post770922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Demon's Total Control and Liar's Tongue be short-circuited by the mind control powers of other splats, like Auspex and the Mind Arcanum?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say (and I think the common ruling) is no. Those are Core Demon features, and can't be circumvented by simple powers. It'd make their ability to hide a joke, were it otherwise the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T22:01:25-08:00","id":771222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=770922#post770922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Demon's Total Control and Liar's Tongue be short-circuited by the mind control powers of other splats, like Auspex and the Mind Arcanum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Liar's Tongue is specifically there to address powers like Auspex and the Mind Arcanum \u2013 it's trippy and unintuitive because that explains how it can get around those powers. (It certainly doesn't do anything when you're dealing with mortal humans without any Supernatural Merits, after all.) It's telling you what happens if a vampire uses Auspex to intuit if the demon believes what he's saying: even when the vampire successfully &quot;reads&quot; the demon's mind, the demon's mind is reflexively fluid and returns whatever answer the demon wants.<br /> <br /> Total Control and Liar's Tongue only address microexpressions, body language, and the demon's ability to cheat at what counts as internal honesty, though. They're anti-sensory bulwarks. They usually do nothing against powers like Dominate and Majesty, or the Telepathic Control spell, though those powers still have to contend with the Unchained's often unusually high Supernatural Tolerance.<br /> <br /> You run into grey areas when powers like these are used to provoke responses relating to these things. If a vampire were to use Dominate to command a demon to tell her the truth behind a given subject, I'd probably say the demon is compelled to answer and give the vampire &quot;the truth,&quot; but the Liar's Tongue still permits the demon to decide on the fly what &quot;the truth&quot; is at the moment (meaning the command becomes pretty useless). If a mage were to cast Emotional Urging on the demon, to evoke, say, a feeling of pity and sympathy, a successful roll would mean the feeling is evoked, but Total Control still permits the demon to decide whether to let that feeling show outwardly. It could be used to nudge the demon's decision making internally, but not to make the demon outwardly crack if he doesn't want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=770922#post770922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'd like some second opinions on my question about clothes and Demonic Form above. In any case, Demons could make clothes that adapt to their Demonic Forms as minor Gadgets, like the outfits of the Fantastic Four.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to assume that the demonic form is unclad (unless you make a point to get a separate wardrobe for it to wear), on the idea that if you switch between Covers from being Janet in marketing to being Mean Lou who works at the auto shop, you're not going to still be wearing Janet's pantsuit. It's one of those things that doesn't have huge bearing, though, so if a player wanted their cool coat to come with from their human form to demonic form, I'd probably just say sure, you can do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T13:35:59-08:00","id":772496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=770922#post770922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Demons don't have any involuntary reactions, are they affected by drunkenness like mortals (i.e. penalty to Mental and Physical, but bonus to Social)? They might get a bonus to fool a drunk person with Subterfuge, I believe. Since they are biologically human when in Cover, I imagine that they can still suffer alcohol poisoning and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Demon would still suffer the full effects of the alcohol, but Total Control would allow them not to display the effects. There brain would be muddled and they would experience dizziness and such, but they wouldn't stumble or slur their words unless they chose too. Granted, being drunk would impair their decision making so they may or may not choose too for the wrong reasons. Also, drinking and not acting drunk would count as a Compromise.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T14:00:55-08:00","id":772510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/655833-questions-about-glitches-and-demonic-powers-i-haven-t-seen-in-other-threads?p=772496#post772496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Demon would still suffer the full effects of the alcohol, but Total Control would allow them not to display the effects. There brain would be muddled and they would experience dizziness and such, but they wouldn't stumble or slur their words unless they chose too. Granted, being drunk would impair their decision making so they may or may not choose too for the wrong reasons. Also, drinking and not acting drunk would count as a Compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/132070845960/standpreg-stardrunk-crusaders-based-off-of\" target=\"_blank\">Relevant</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}